Venetium 0059 - a built-in ad and tracker blocker (subresource_filter + EasyList/EasyPrivacy), on by default.
From the performance research (C:\handoff\PERF-RESEARCH.md, item N2), his decision 2026-10-15 ("include, on by
default"). On a 1.3 GHz Cortex-A9 the scripts of ad and tracker networks are seconds of main-thread CPU per page.
Chromium's subresource_filter (the Better Ads / abusive-ads blocker) was compiled in and idle: its presets need Safe
Browsing lists this build has no key for, and its all-sites preset is a dry run.
- components/subresource_filter/core/browser/subresource_filter_features.{h,cc}: a preset
  "venetium_live_run_on_all_sites" (enabled by default): activation level enabled, scope all sites, priority 2000 (above
  every stock preset). A site the user allows ads on (the "Ads" site setting, or "Always allow ads on this site" in
  the blocked-ads bubble) is not filtered (ProfileInteractionManager, stock). Off everywhere:
  --disable-features=SubresourceFilter, or SubresourceFilter:disable_presets/venetium_live_run_on_all_sites.
- chrome/browser/browser_process_impl.cc: when the RulesetService is created, read venetium_filters\version.txt next to
  the executable (off the UI thread) and hand venetium_filters\filters.dat (+ LICENSE.txt) to
  RulesetService::IndexAndStoreAndPublishRulesetIfNeeded, which indexes it once per content version on a background
  thread after startup and keeps publishing the stored indexed copy on later launches. No list next to the exe = no
  blocking (stock behaviour).
- The list itself is not in this patch: venetium_filters\filters.dat is built at packaging time from EasyList +
  EasyPrivacy (https://easylist.to/, GPLv3 / CC BY-SA 3.0, see venetium_filters\LICENSE.txt) by
  components/subresource_filter/tools:ruleset_converter (network rules only; no element hiding or scriptlets), see
  RECIPE.md. 0058 stops registering Google's ruleset component so it cannot replace it.
Risk: site breakage from network rules (the per-site allow is the escape hatch); one-time indexing CPU after install and
after each list update.

